      "content": "But you're kind of sidestepping the core problem. If the state is using secret mass surveillance, how can there even be \"consent\" or \"transparency\"? If the people don't know what's happening, the contract is basically a lie. \n\nIsn't it more accurate to say that massive surveillance is a total abandonment of the social contract, rather than an \"evolution\" of it? The \"evolution\" argument feels like a way to just excuse state overreach.",
